<title>ESTONIA: LOW LIQUIDITY RAISES SHORT-TERM INTERBANK RATES.</title>
<headline>LOW LIQUIDITY RAISES SHORT-TERM INTERBANK RATES.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Short-term average interbank</p>
<p>rates rose on Wednesday with long-term rates remaining</p>
<p>unchanged, the central bank said on Wenesday.</p>
<p>A money market analyst said liquidity was low on the market</p>
<p>and the rates are expected to rise further next week unless</p>
<p>some resources are brought to the market.</p>
<p>    TALIBOR/TALIBID   1Week	 1Month    3Month</p>
<p>  July 16	    4.28/3.28  5.50/4.50  7.00/6.00</p>
<p>  July 09	    4.23/3.23  5.43/4.43  7.00/6.00</p>
